    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5062\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to directing the\ncommission to establish standards and safeguards for certain radio and\nphone providers to meet eligibility to provide lifeline services\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo establish standards and safeguards by the Public Service Commission\nwhen approving as an eligible telecommunications carrier for the\npurposes of providing lifeline service.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends paragraph c of subdivision 6 of section 5 of the\npublic service law.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLast year, the Legislature passed, and the Governor signed into law a\nbill that granted the New York State Public Service Commission authority\nto grant eligible telecommunications carrier (ETC) designations to wire-\nless telecommunications providers. This program is known as the \"Life-\nline\" program and provides subsidized telecommunications services to\nlow-income individuals.\n\nIn order to ensure that that reputable companies are entering into the\nLifeline program; it is vital that the PSC has the authority to estab-\nlish standards and safeguards to properly check new ETCs before receiv-\ning designation in the Lifeline program to provide essential services to\nNew Yorkers.\n\nJust this year, State regulators in Oklahoma looked to revoke the ETC\ndesignation of a company doing business in the state due to a consistent\ntrack-record of violations and illegally obtaining customers. This\nlegislation will provide the proper mechanisms to make sure that custom-\ners under the Lifeline program are not being taken advantage of by bad\nactors.\n\nhttp://www.okenergytoday.com/2020/02/state- regulators-seek-suspension-\noft rue-wireless-over-alleged-lifeline-fraud/\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
